        "payload": "tree 5394446d6379df0396022c68b84ea513a5f0e501\nparent ec17e281bc1e5c235da1a0fa085c8f46ff4f4685\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790629562 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790629562 +0000\n\nsituations: playable quilt situations projecting JEV fold + Moth draw (S17 runnable)\n\nDesign doc arch/PLAYABLE-SITUATIONS.md + runnable play/weakest-leaf.mjs.\nS17 \"The Weakest Leaf\" plays live: decomposing JEV noul-fold localizes a tool's\nweakest advertised guarantee, Moth's CHSH-witnessed (S=2.82) quantum draw fires an\nun-gameable adversary at it. Played vs lever-runner: located L5 \"LLM never sees\nabsolute paths\" as the most overclaimed leaf; whole overclaims uniformly so the\nranking (argmin), not the level, is the signal.\n\nAlso books the live-schema correction: Moth derive body is params.derive.integers\n(top-level 422s); draws at random.derived.integers.values, seed at random.hex.\n\nSynergy verdicts: exoj (STRONG, the non-collapsing surface the fold wants),\npincher/pincher4jev (STRONG structural, the deadband to instrument), lever-runner\n(EXISTS; the first audit target), constraint-theory-core (MEDIUM, the deadband math).\nS18 (pincher gate calibration) + S19 (un-gameable curriculum) designed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JV2C8fnD86DNwXoyHPd7X9\n",
